Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Sable Attention and per-app Sable Hub entries

DESIGN-KF-A Settings information architecture: keep Android's
notification structure and add two links into Sable Hub, which owns only
Hub aggregation and Sable hardware-attention preferences.

* Settings > Notifications > Sable Attention opens
  org.sableos.hub.action.ATTENTION_SETTINGS.
* App notifications > (app) > Sable Hub and Attention opens
  org.sableos.hub.action.APP_NOTIFICATION_SETTINGS with the package and
  uid, so work-profile apps keep their own entry.

Both entries are hidden when Sable Hub is not installed. Delivery,
channels, conversations, lock screen and Do Not Disturb stay on these
Android pages; Hub keeps no copy of them.
